=> Jacobi holds iff c(1 + n alpha) = 1 - alpha.
   alpha=0 (fundamental u(n) action): c = 1
   alpha=1 (sl_{n+1} action):          c = 0
   c = 1/2 (with alpha = 0) is NOT a Lie bracket.

check of the general solution c = (1-alpha)/(1+n alpha):
   n=2 alpha=1/2 c=1/4 : max|Jacobi| = 0
   n=2 alpha=3/2 c=-1/8 : max|Jacobi| = 0
